From d75ef01b72ebdcd79b6905ace73ba22ae9b8c1d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:09:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/49] x86_64/mic: generic C for the remaining SSE string
 functions

memrchr, wcschr, wcscmp, wcslen, wcsrchr, and wmemset/__wmemset_chk
(implemented in the SSE2 memset.S since 2.26), and since 2.35 __memcmpeq
(an alias of the generic memcmp) and wmemcmp, since 2.39 the
stpcpy/strcpy/strcat/strncat/strncpy/stpncpy and wide-character families
(multiarch SSE2 code included from sysdeps/x86_64).  micgen.py lists
them.  Intel moved the SSE2 versions out of sysdeps/x86_64 so that K1OM
fell back to the generic C code; since sysdeps/x86_64/mic precedes
sysdeps/x86_64, overriding them there does the same without touching the
x86_64 files (which no longer apply after the 2.26 multiarch rework).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
